XB-Kidux-Name-en: ScratchJr
XB-Kidux-Description-en: Stories and games with blocks, without a word to read, for the youngest.
XB-Kidux-Name-es: ScratchJr
XB-Kidux-Description-es: Historias y juegos con bloques, sin una palabra que leer, para los más pequeños.
XB-Kidux-Ages: 5-7
Description: Kidux learning module: ScratchJr, stories and games with blocks for the youngest
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module is ScratchJr, MIT's programming app for children of five to seven:
 characters move, talk and play by blocks snapped together, without a word
 to read. It is the community's desktop port of MIT's own app, with the
 Electron it runs in. A child's projects are kept in their Documents.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
